translate(64.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_17\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(91.65131 98.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(65.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_18\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(131.441899 71.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_19\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(170.278582 83.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(65.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_20\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(209.383039 140.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(64.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_21\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(248.924605 113.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_22\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(287.961679 56.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_23\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(327.480979 20.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_24\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(366.461217 14.445) scale(0.075 -0.075)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(66.796875 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pa45bfe94e6\"><rect x=\"41.311438\" y=\"14.145\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Fjord EBITDA ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>EBITDA swings between $38M and $80M. The nine-year average is about <b>$58.2M</b>, so this year is about 37% above average, near the top of the cycle.</p>"},{"q":"If the fund pays $640M and EBITDA returns to its average by exit, what return does it make?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Equity in: $640M − $400M debt = $240M. Exit: $58.2M × 7 = $408M; less $300M debt = <b>$108M</b>.</p> <p>Return: <b>0.45×</b>. The fund loses money, even though Fjord stays profitable.</p>"},{"q":"What happens to the debt in a downturn like the last one?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>At the last trough EBITDA was $38M. With $400M of debt, leverage would be <b>10.5×</b>, far above the 4–6× where lenders usually step in. The fund could lose control of the company.</p>"},{"q":"What would you bid?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Start from mid-cycle earnings and debt the business can survive: about 3.5× $58.2M = $204M.</p> <p>Even 8× mid-cycle ($466M) returns only about 1.2× when the exit is at 7×. For 2.5×: exit equity $58.2M × 7 − ($204M − $100M repaid) = $304M, so equity in can be at most $122M and the price at most <b>about $325M</b> (5.6× mid-cycle EBITDA).</p> <p>Even that debt would be about 5.4× EBITDA at a trough like the last one, at the edge of what lenders accept, so treat $325M as a ceiling, not a target.</p> <p>That is half the asking price, so the owners will refuse. Be ready to walk away, or wait and bid in the downturn.</p>"}],"reco":"Don't bid $640M. This year's $80M of EBITDA is near the top of the cycle; the nine-year average is about $58.2M. Paying 8× peak earnings and exiting at average earnings returns about 0.45× the fund's money, and $400M of debt would reach 10.5× EBITDA in a downturn like the last one. To reach 2.5× with safe debt, the fund could pay at most about $325M, half the asking price, so walk away now and look again in the downturn. Next step: model the next three years from the ship order book.","great":["Recognises a cyclical business and normalises earnings","Shows that buying at the peak destroys returns","Stress-tests leverage at the trough","Works back to a maximum price and is willing to walk away"],"id":70,"slug":"fjord-chemicals"}